ounty","/arc-plc/florida/escambia-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 shows September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. In 2026 so far, March to April sat at 30% of normal on the middle, and May to June at 155%. Grid 12472 had its driest year in 1954 at 47% of normal.</p>"}
